From 1ab0e3712fb5ecc6afe3a014cc0fdf24bde8d9ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:03:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] web: Mode Ladder, one Speed Ramp switch, Activated sensor
 modes

Why: the ladder needs an editor, and the T32 Speed Ramp block asked for
more than Patrik uses (he wants one switch: FPS may change while
recording).

What: Settings > Record gets three cards from the approved mockup. Mode
Ladder: Activate ladder switch, the running line, the resolutions with
drag and drop, "Up to" FPS, compression per resolution, file size per
frame and per second, crop diagrams in Cinemate's style from the probe's
crop rectangles, an FPS coverage bar, Save and Revert; Core checks every
draft with a dry run and illegal values cannot be entered. Speed Ramp:
one "Allow speed ramping" switch (the T32 block's shutter sync, ramp
targets and actions are removed). Activated sensor modes: the probe's
modes with filters and Add. Camera settings: "Resolution N" under each
FPS pill, the running line next to Frame rate, resolution and crop pills
locked while the ladder picks the mode; the same lock in Recording
format and in the Favorites format card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T93jucKMhWYnQM1yyFVkbH
